<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Anhalt</h1><p class="st-meta">1863 CE – 1918 CE · capital Dessau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Duchy that reunited the Anhalt lands in 1863 and became an industrial region on the Elbe and Saale.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the extinction of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt-kothen">Anhalt-Köthen</a> in 1847 and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt-bernburg">Anhalt-Bernburg</a> in 1863, Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-iv-duke-of-anhalt">Leopold IV Frederick</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt-dessau">Anhalt-Dessau</a> ruled all the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt">Anhalt</a> territories. In 1863 they were formally combined as the Duchy of Anhalt, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a> as capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt">Anhalt</a> was small but economically active, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> beet, lignite, potash and salt, and later chemical and engineering works. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-junkers">Hugo Junkers</a> founded his first works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a> in 1895, later the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/junkers">Junkers</a> aircraft factory. A constitution of 1859, extended to the whole duchy, provided a diet. Anhalt joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-german-confederation">North German Confederation</a> in 1867 and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a> in 1871.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joachim-ernst-duke-of-anhalt">Joachim Ernst</a>, a minor, abdicated through his regent in November 1918, and the duchy became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-anhalt">Free State of Anhalt</a>. After 1945 its territory was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, which still takes its name in part from the old duchy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-anhalt.jpg" alt="Duchy of Anhalt" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Herzogtum_Anhalt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1863 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dessau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Leopold IV Frederick, Frederick I, Joachim Ernst</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Herzogtum Anhalt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=duchy-of-anhalt" aria-label="Duchy of Anhalt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4956 385 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Anhalt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5276 641L5276 641M5276 641L5265 642M5276 641L5300 622M5276 641L5300 622M5276 641L5276 641"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5276 641h0M5265 642h0M5300 622h0M5300 622h0M5276 641h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5276 641h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5276 641h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dessau. <a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=duchy-of-anhalt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
